### CHECK constraint via the check() operator

Source: https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm-docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/pg/indexes-constraints.mdx

Declares a table-level CHECK constraint with a raw SQL expression using the standalone check() operator from drizzle-orm/pg-core.

```typescript
// Check
import { sql } from "drizzle-orm";
import { check, integer, pgTable, text, uuid } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

export const users = pgTable(
  "users",
  {
    id: uuid().defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
    username: text().notNull(),
    age: integer(),
  },
  (table) => [
    check("age_check1", sql`${table.age} > 21`),
  ]
);
```

