### Specify custom TypeScript types with jsonb().$type()

Source: https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm-docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/cockroach/column-types.mdx

Applies compile-time type inference for JSON object values without performing runtime validation. Provides type safety for default values, insert schemas, and select schemas.

```typescript
// will be inferred as { foo: string }
jsonb: jsonb().$type<{ foo: string }>();

// will be inferred as string[]
jsonb: jsonb().$type<string[]>();

// won't compile
jsonb: jsonb().$type<string[]>().default({});
```

--------------------------------

### PostgreSQL jsonb with $type for compile-time type inference

Source: https://github.com/drizzle-team/drizzle-orm-docs/blob/main/src/content/docs/pg/column-types.mdx

Demonstrates how to use jsonb() with $type<>() in PostgreSQL for type-safe JSON columns. $type provides compile-time inference for default values, insert and select schemas but does not affect runtime values or the generated SQL schema.

```typescript
// will be inferred as { foo: string }
jsonb: jsonb().$type<{ foo: string }>();

// will be inferred as string[]
jsonb: jsonb().$type<string[]>();

// won't compile
jsonb: jsonb().$type<string[]>().default({});
```

