```

`lines` from the map is `PricingSnapshotLine[]` (union) since spread of union… Actually `baseline.lines.map(...)` — baseline.lines typed `PricingSnapshotLinePayloadV2[] | PricingSnapshotLinePayloadV3[]`? In the union type, accessing `.lines` gives union of array types → `.map` may complain "each member has signatures but none compatible". Hmm. TS union of arrays: calling map on `A[] | B[]` — TS 5 supports calling union of same-signature methods? It's an error historically ("This expression is not callable. Each member of the union type ... has signatures, but none of those signatures are compatible with each other"). Actually for arrays of different element types, `union.map` gives error. Safer: type `const baseLines: readonly PricingSnapshotLine[] = baseline.lines;` — assignment from `A[]|B[]` to union-element array is fine (covariant). Then map on that.

